  "details": "1: In the open beta, load into a world that contains a DXT1 texture with a texture resolution that isn't a power of 4 (see the example world)\n\n2: The game will crash.\n\nThis seems to be a bug in the editor of Unity 2019.4.31f1 allowing you to create invalid DXT1 textures, though I haven't checked if this is fixed in 2022.3.5f1's editor.\n\nIf you take a 4x4 texture and set its texture shape to Cube, its resolution will be halved to 2x2 - and since DXT1 requires texture resolutions in powers of 4, this becomes an invalid texture.\n\nOrdinarily, Unity will prevent you from making a DXT1 texture with a resolution that isn't a power of 4, but the Cube texture shape seems to bypass this check.\n\nOn the live version of VRChat, the game will throw an error similar to the following into the output log, without crashing:\n\n`Texture 'sky_Texture' has dimensions 2 x 2 which is not supported for format 'RGB Compressed DXT1|BC1' (requires multiple-of-four dimensions). Falling back to 'RGBA 32 bit'.`\n\nOn the open beta, that error will also be thrown, but the game will also crash.\n\nHere's an example world: https://vrch.at/8wp08x26\n\nThis issue seems to only be present in worlds from my testing; *avatars* with invalid DXT1 textures throw the above error, but don't crash the game.",
